name = pyxb.binding.basis.element(pyxb.namespace.ExpandedName(_Namespace_gml, 'name'), CodeType, documentation='The gml:name property provides a label or identifier for the object, commonly a descriptive name. An object may have several names, typically assigned by different authorities. gml:name uses the gml:CodeType content model.  The authority for a name is indicated by the value of its (optional) codeSpace attribute.  The name may or may not be unique, as determined by the rules of the organization responsible for the codeSpace.  In common usage there will be one name per authority, so a processing application may select the name from its preferred codeSpace.', location=pyxb.utils.utility.Location('http://schemas.opengis.net/gml/3.2.1/gmlBase.xsd', 127, 1))
